.Dd November 18, 2026
.Dt USB-HID 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm usb-hid
.Nd USB HID boot-keyboard console queue
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
serves the
.Dq kbd:
scheme over the bounded console input queue.
The xHCI driver pushes decoded boot-keyboard ASCII with
.Dv WRITE
and a reader drains it with
.Dv READ .
An empty queue returns
.Er EAGAIN
and a full queue returns
.Er ENOSPC ;
bytes are never silently overwritten.
The queue holds 256 bytes.
.Pp
The service is optional.
With no keyboard attached it stays up with an empty queue and does not gate
UART getty or login.
The US layout is selected first.
Modifiers, Enter, Backspace and Ctrl-D map to the console bytes documented in
.Pa docs/pi4-usb.md .
A non-keyboard HID descriptor is rejected before it reaches the queue.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/usb-hid.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/usb-hid.toml
Service manifest staged in the Pi 4 release profile.
.El
